CloudBurrow patch 1 of 6 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1.

Not CloudBurrow's work: this is goccy/googlesqlite pull request #76,
"value: cast ARRAY elements and nested STRUCT fields against the declared
type", by Masaaki Goshima (@goccy), the project's author, at its head commit
63e6793e1f7994d80e40bc3b976fac1889aaebf0, unchanged
(https://github.com/goccy/googlesqlite/pull/76). It is open upstream, not
merged or released; it is applied here until a googlesqlite release carries
it. It applies to v0.3.1 without change and builds against the go-googlesql
v0.3.0 that bigquery-emulator v0.8.1 pins.

Why CloudBurrow carries it (cloudburrow/cloudburrow#900, #1061): a value in a
RECORD inside a REPEATED RECORD, streamed or loaded, left the table
unreadable ("failed to convert struct from array").

Licence: googlesqlite is under the MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Masaaki
Goshima (third_party/bigquery-emulator/licenses/googlesqlite.LICENSE); the
